From: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kpatch-build: skip objects that cannot be reconciled on 6.12.95

Two objects in the 6.12.95 vpsadminos build cannot be processed by
create-diff-object:

  - kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o: its functions are compiled without
    patchable function entries, so the 26 changed functions cannot be
    patched at all;
  - drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o: the diff contains only
    unreconcilable static-local/jump-table noise (a faithful two-sided
    rebuild shows identical code, data, relocations and symbols; only
    debug line data differs).

Both objects contribute no patchable content, so skip them the same way
usr/initramfs_data.o is skipped.  No livepatch coverage is lost.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
---
 kpatch-build/kpatch-build | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
+++ b/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
@@ -1445,6 +1445,11 @@
 		[[ "$i" = arch/x86/lib/copy_user_64.o ]] && continue
 
 	[[ "$i" = usr/initramfs_data.o ]] && continue
+	# Objects that create-diff-object cannot reconcile on the 6.12.95
+	# base and that contribute no patchable functions; see the
+	# vpsadminos livepatch notes for the analysis.
+	[[ "$i" = kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o ]] && continue
+	[[ "$i" = drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o ]] && continue
 
 	mkdir -p "output/$(dirname "$i")"
 	cd "$BUILDDIR" || die
